Subject: [PATCH 50/73] feat(gauntlet-tdd): distribute the gauntlet
 RED-to-GREEN loop as a pack (gcp-dnxq)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

No pack in this repo shipped a TDD or contract-test workflow, so the gauntlet
CLI's scaffold -> red -> implement -> green cycle was something each rig
re-derived by hand. This packages it: one formula, mol-tdd-red-green, that
takes a bead id, scaffolds a contract from that bead's acceptance criteria,
proves the contract RED, routes implementation to the rig's implementer, and
proves it GREEN.

The design turns on one inversion that is easy to get backwards and silent
when you do. `gauntlet scaffold --from-bead` emits skip-guarded stubs, and a
skipped test is not a failed test, so `gauntlet run local` exits 0 on a
brand-new scaffold. Measured on the gaunt-8ibp smoke, same tree, same moment:
run local gave `pass=0 fail=0 skipped=3` and exit 0, while `gauntlet lint`
gave exit 1 and three `todo_skip` findings. A formula that proved red with
run local would therefore certify an EMPTY contract and wave every later step
through — an inverted gate, not merely a weak one. So `gauntlet lint` is the
red gate here, `run local` is the green gate, and the test suite asserts
neither can drift into the other's job. The green gate additionally rejects
`skipped != 0`, which is the same hole seen from the other side.

The lane is pinned to bats. A bead-scoped run dispatches by file extension
via inferTool, so a `.bats` covering file structurally never reaches the hurl
runner — which is what keeps the gauntlet repo's two open hurl-corpus defects
(gaunt-4bzz, gaunt-svhp) off this pack's path. Every run passes
`--contracts=bats` explicitly and the suite asserts no step names the hurl
lane, so that stays an enforced invariant rather than a property of today's
scaffold output.

Routing: only the implement step is routed, via
`gc.run_target = "{{implementer_target}}"`, defaulting to `gastown.polecat`.
`gc.run_target` reaches only roles the consuming rig actually imports, and the
gauntlet rig imports gastown plus its own crew pack — the twelve winnow-only
build-pack roles are unavailable there. Hence one routed step to one role
every gastown-importing rig has, overridable with `--implementer`. The suite
asserts every step target a formula names is documented in the README as a
required import, so a new routed role cannot be added silently.

`gauntlet loop --bead <id>` already runs this cycle in one process and is
deliberately NOT wrapped: its `--exec` model drives implementation as an
opaque subprocess, invisible to the witness and the refinery. The gc dispatch
is the point. The README names it as the local single-process equivalent.

Validation:
- gauntlet-tdd/tests: 17 passed, 15 subtests. Mutation-checked, not just run —
  swapping the red gate to run local, switching the green run to the hurl
  lane, and pointing implementer_target at an undocumented role each turn the
  suite red.
- Full CI pytest path list (with gauntlet-tdd/tests appended): 832 passed,
  7 skipped, 9447 subtests. Two gascity claim-command failures are
  pre-existing — reproduced at the untouched merge-base bb1800f in a separate
  worktree — and are filed as gcp-yafz.
- `gc lint gauntlet-tdd`: ok.
- `gc import check` against the documented stanza in a scratch city: exit 0,
  "Import state OK", with `gc import list` resolving ../packs/gauntlet-tdd.
- End-to-end smoke on the gauntlet rig, bead gaunt-8ibp, bats lane: scaffold
  emitted a 3-stub .bats; lint exit 1 (findings=3); after implementation lint
  exit 0 and a bead-scoped run gave total=3 pass=3 fail=0 skipped=0.

ci.yml's pytest path list is explicit, not a glob, so `gauntlet-tdd/tests` is
appended there in this commit — without it the suite would ship green locally
and never run in CI.

The registry entry follows in a separate commit: validate_registry.py
recomputes each release hash from `git ls-tree` at the named commit, so the
pack subtree has to exist in history before it can be pinned.
